<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Background tint for the buy-credit segmented toggles (duration + pay rail).
  Checked = a TONAL fill; unchecked = transparent, so "selected" reads from
  FILL-VERSUS-OUTLINE rather than from saturation, and the brand fill stays
  unique to the one primary action on the screen (Continue).

  Two things it must NOT be, both tried:

  - The default outlined MaterialButton checked state, a colorPrimary overlay:
    a loud coral block indistinguishable from the CTA.
  - ?attr/colorSecondaryContainer, and then @color/chip_checked_container.
    Those fail for opposite reasons that land in the same place. The token has
    no real dark container tone in this palette (#FFA8A0 at L* 77 — a LIGHT
    fill in night mode), so the checked segment measured 10.04:1 against the
    dark page while the CTA below it was 6.44:1 — the mode selector out-shouting
    the button it feeds. Moving it to the checked-chip tone fixed that
    inversion but not the hierarchy: at ΔE 8.2 (light) / 5.9 (dark) from
    #f0716c, segment and CTA still read as one colour. The chip can afford the
    brand because a list rail has no primary action to be subordinate to; this
    control does not have that luxury.

  @color/buy_segment_checked_container is ΔE 48.3 (light) / 55.6 (dark) from
  the CTA — unmistakably not the button, still unmistakably selected.

  The stroke stays @color/buy_segment_stroke (outlineVariant) in every state,
  so the group keeps reading as one segmented unit.
-->
<selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:state_checked="true" android:color="@color/buy_segment_checked_container" />
    <item android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
</selector>
